                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you like jigsaw puzzle games, I recommend this game.  I used to play the board game that this is based on, Psyche-paths, so I admit I bought this for nostalgia as much as any other reason.  (I got it during the Steam Winter Sale for about half off, and I think that it was worth it.)  Even so, it is a decent jigsaw puzzle game where you have to keep swapping around hexagonal tiles until you solve it by having all the colors be in their own loops.   \n\nBesides tile-swapping, other mechanics include tiles that are fixed in place but rotate and tiles that are fixed in place but change colors.  I ignore both and just do all the edges first-- a few seconds of perusing the tiles to see which must-- simply must!-- go on top or bottom saves hours later on.  \n\nSadly, the bonus goldfish level isn't available in Vermont.  \n\nOtherwise, a solid thumbs up!",
